    ``CUexecAffinitySmCount``. This limit will be internally rounded up to the
    next hardware-supported amount. Hence, it is imperative to query the actual
    execution affinity of the context via ``cuCtxGetExecAffinity`` after
    context creation. Currently, this attribute is only supported under Volta+
    MPS.

    A CUDA context can be created in CIG(CUDA in Graphics) mode by setting
    ``cigParams``. Data from graphics client is shared with CUDA via the
    ``sharedData`` in ``cigParams``. Support for D3D12 graphics client can be
    determined using :func:`device_get_attribute` with
