    value returned in ``*data`` will equal the input value ``ptr``.

    - ``CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_HOST_POINTER``:.

    - Returns in ``*data`` the host pointer value through which ``ptr`` may be
    accessed by by the host program. The type of ``data`` must be void **. If
    there exists no host pointer value through which the host program may
    directly access ``ptr`` then ``CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE`` is returned.

